Interpret actual departure and access-status events under supplied sharing rules. Minimize capture to evidence needed by this handover's open obligations. An access revocation changes what can be fetched; it does not erase a legitimately retained snapshot. Accept a frozen source only with its capture time, edition and authorization receipt. Missing receipt means a capture request, not a claimed snapshot. For personal notes, ask the author for the smallest relevant passage; never copy mailbox or notebook content wholesale.
